A||||3||XDrewX||84 4:10 tranny  swap to 86 4 speed question||||1||
Z||000000||XDrewX||12-04-2001||01:54 PM||||I was reading an article in an old "Big Fiero Book"  it was by Associated Auto.<P>They article stated:<P>You can swap an 84 4:10 geared tranny with a 85-86 4 spd and reuse all cables, mounts, slave etc.<BR>They supposedly bolt right up.<BR>They did not mention the actual shifter "stick".<P>Has anyone done this, and if so are the above statements true.<BR>What do you do about the shifter?<P>Thanks<P>Andrew<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||12-04-2001||08:16 PM||||Yes, all you need to swap in the car is the 4 spd itself. Everything off the 3.65 4spd will bolt right on.<BR> <BR> The only differences in the 84 4 spds and the newer ones are all internal in transaxle case.<BR> <BR> Shifters and cables, mounts and the brackets are the same, just use the slave and the slave mount from which ever car you are putting this in. <P> The 84 clutch is the same as used in the 85-85 V6  4spds.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-04-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||12-05-2001||09:40 AM||||It has also been proven that the magical 4.10 cog can be put into the 85-86 tranny case.  There has been some debate on if the 84 tranny case can be used over a long period of time. ||||reg||2
Z||000003||jelly2m8||12-06-2001||02:21 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>It has also been proven that the magical 4.10 cog can be put into the 85-86 tranny case.  There has been some debate on if the 84 tranny case can be used over a long period of time. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya, sorry I didn't get too specific there, most people don't like to look inside these things.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016084.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016084.html</A> <P> See this tread I posted about the shift forks being larger and a little different. in the 85-86's. Gear sets are interchangable, as is the differential assembly.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
